   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "Note"
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "HOW TO USE (Flat2VR with MiniMax-H3-Image: a 2D photo into a VR180 image)\n\n1. Drop your photo onto Flat2VR Place Photo and place it (drag = move, scroll = size, Shift = crop).\n2. Flat2VR Prompt (optional): setting, position, POV body. Keep \"label_no_body\" ON for this LoRA.\n3. Run. Pass 1 makes the left eye at 2048 (6 steps, cfg 1). The hi-res fix scales it to 4096, re-renders it there\n   (from sigma 0.53: start_at_step 4; 5 = lighter, 3 = stronger) and decodes at 4096, so H3's\n   compressed VAE gets the room for fine detail; then it goes back to 2048 and the photo is pasted back exactly.\n4. The Qwen l2r LoRA makes the right eye from that; both side by side are saved as flat2vr_h3_180_LR_*.png\n   (2048 per eye). The 4096 left eye has a save node that is off (bypassed): select it, Ctrl+B to switch it on.\n\nFirst knobs if the refined eye drifts from pass 1 (moved photo, grey bleeding back, repeated structure):\nstart_at_step 5, then the refine LoRA strength. Check the console for 'lora key not loaded' on the first run.\n\nModels: H3 needs minimax_h3_image_pruned_int8_convrot.safetensors, qwen3vl_32b_minimax_h3_nvfp4_awq.safetensors (CLIP type minimax) and minimax_h3_image_vae_fp16.safetensors;\nthe right eye uses the Qwen-Image 2.1 files, as in qwen.json. Both sets load in turn; ComfyUI swaps them."
   ],
   "title": "How to use",
   "color": "#444"
  },
